[
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"448405\">Alex Meiburg</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Notation.20classes.20on.20.60Type.20_.60.20only/near/599570180\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Anyway, is there a particular reason that notations like HMul <em>don't</em> support Prop?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yes, limiting operations to <code>Type _</code> only greatly simplifies the universe level handling, and this simplifies the job of the elaborator. To see this, compare the resulting universe of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Sigma#doc\">docs#Sigma</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=PSigma#doc\">docs#PSigma</a>.<br>\nThe problem with <code>PSigma</code> is that the resulting universe contains universe expressions such as <code>max 1 u</code>. These are not nice to work with, since they're not injective as function of <code>u</code>. In particular, neither of the unification problems <code>max 1 ?u =?= max 1 v</code> and <code>max 1 ?u =?= 1</code> have unique solutions.</p>\n<p>Back in Lean 2 (I believe) type formers accepted <code>Sort _</code> arguments by default which often worked fine, but also quite regularly required explicit universe annotations that are almost never necessary when using the type-valued versions.</p>",
        "id": 599810317,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1780495494
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"111080\">Floris van Doorn</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Notation.20classes.20on.20.60Type.20_.60.20only/near/599810317\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The problem with <code>PSigma</code> is that the resulting universe contains universe expressions such as <code>max 1 u</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>note that it is technically possible to write a version of <code>PSigma</code> that has type <code>{α : Sort u} → (β : α → Sort v) → Sort (max u v)</code>, which would presumably fix this problem</p>",
        "id": 599811336,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780495744
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks, I had read the docstring on PSigma several times on the past but never understood concretely what \"this generality leads to universe level constraints that are difficult to solve\" was trying to imply.</p>\n<p>Why would extending HMul to Prop lead to this issue, though? I thought this was only an issue with structures.</p>",
        "id": 599815199,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1780496602
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Notation.20classes.20on.20.60Type.20_.60.20only/near/599811336\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>note that it is technically possible to write a version of <code>PSigma</code> that has type <code>{α : Sort u} → (β : α → Sort v) → Sort (max u v)</code>, which would presumably fix this problem</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can you explain? I mean, Lean simply doesn't allow structures of universe <code>max u v</code> because then it can't tell whether you get large elimination or not. Do you mean that Lean's machinery could be altered to permit this without affecting the type theory? Or that there's some kind of elaborator-level hacks that would let you imitate a <code>Sort (max u v)</code>?</p>",
        "id": 599821397,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1780497386
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"448405\">Alex Meiburg</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Notation.20classes.20on.20.60Type.20_.60.20only/near/599821397\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Notation.20classes.20on.20.60Type.20_.60.20only/near/599811336\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>note that it is technically possible to write a version of <code>PSigma</code> that has type <code>{α : Sort u} → (β : α → Sort v) → Sort (max u v)</code>, which would presumably fix this problem</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can you explain? I mean, Lean simply doesn't allow structures of universe <code>max u v</code> because then it can't tell whether you get large elimination or not. Do you mean that Lean's machinery could be altered to permit this without affecting the type theory? Or that there's some kind of elaborator-level hacks that would let you imitate a <code>Sort (max u v)</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I mean there's some hacky stuff you can do to permit this without modifying Lean itself</p>",
        "id": 599822021,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780497513
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>unfortunately it breaks a lot of automation</p>",
        "id": 599822048,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780497520
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>here's the stuff</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>stuff</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bootstrap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inductiveCheckResultingUniverse</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">genSizeOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">genInjectivity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst_mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd_mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>",
        "id": 599824015,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780497974
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that \"the stuff\" results in <code>PSigma'.rec</code> eliminating into prop alone; but we can write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rec'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">},</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rec'_mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">PSigma'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rec'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 599831075,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780499454
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe that's worth a thread or issue, I don't see why PSigma doesn't live in that simpler universe</p>",
        "id": 599831656,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780499580
    },
